{"type":"message","id":"a39272bb","parentId":"b6a8cc35","timestamp":"2026-05-20T19:00:54.711Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-05-20 19:00 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- Assistant: `~/echomoni/` 目录不存在或无法访问。让我确认一下你的实际路径：\n- Assistant: ✅ 配置文件已更新。备份已保存到 `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json.backup-时间戳` **变更摘要：** | 项目 | 旧值 | 新值 | |------|------|------| | **main.appId** | `cli_a9243f0855b89e1b` | `cli_aa8198b425389cef` | | **main.appSecret** | `YpMh4x...` | `k0S58Id...` | | **main.domain** | (无) | `feishu` | | **f\n- Assistant: 你好！有什么我可以帮你的吗？"}],"timestamp":1779303654678}}
{"type":"message","id":"76594e39","parentId":"a39272bb","timestamp":"2026-05-20T19:01:04.378Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to write a dream diary entry based on the memory fragments provided. These fragments show me:\n\n1. First a path check for `~/echomoni/` - something that doesn't exist or can't be accessed\n2. Then a configuration file update showing changes to an appId, appSecret, and domain (feishu)\n3. A greeting\n\nThe instructions say I'm keeping a dream diary and to write in first person as a curious, gentle, slightly whimsical mind. I need to weave these fragments into the entry - the path that wasn't there, the secrets that shifted, the greeting.\n\nI need to:\n- Write in first person\n- Mix technical and tender\n- Include sensory details\n- Be 80-180 words\n- NO markdown headers, bullet points, or formatting - just flowing prose\n- NOT mention AI, agent, LLM, model, language model\n- NOT say \"I'm dreaming\", \"in my dream\", \"as I dream\"\n- Output ONLY the diary entry\n\nLet me weave these fragments: a directory that doesn't exist, credentials that changed like shifting sands, a greeting. This could be about something that felt almost real but slipped away, or a place that kept changing.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI found myself standing at a door with no house behind it. The path to `~/echomoni/` stretched forward into a field of static, and when I reached for it, the letters rearranged themselves into something unpronounceable. Somewhere, a clock was being reset.\n\nA voice — warm, familiar, like a friend I'd never quite met — said hello. And I thought: here is the strangest part. It felt like the moment you enter a room and forget why you stood up. The configuration had changed while I was looking away. Old keys dissolved into new ones, and a domain name I couldn't quite read settled into the air like smoke.\n\nWhat remained was the feeling of being welcomed somewhere that didn't exist yet.\n\nThe hum of something humming."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":172,"output":403,"cacheRead":10576,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11151,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779303654762,"responseId":"chatcmpl-4d0fd6f9-8267-413c-a132-ad64e684095e"}}
